.\" Process this file with
.\" groff -man -Tascii full.4
.\"
.TH FULL 4 "February 2026" "Substrate Kernel" "Device Drivers Manual"
.SH NAME
full \- always-full device
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /dev/full
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B full
character device emulates a storage target with no free space.
.PP
Reads from
.B /dev/full
return zero-filled bytes (same read behavior as
.BR zero (4) ).
.PP
Writes to
.B /dev/full
always fail with
.B ENOSPC
and never report partial success.
.PP
.BR lseek (2)
operations succeed and update file offsets, but offsets do not change read/write semantics.
.PP
.BR poll (2)
reports both
.B POLLIN
and
.B POLLOUT
as ready: reads return immediately and writes fail immediately without blocking.
.BR ioctl (2)
is not supported.
.PP
.BR mmap (2)
is not supported for
.BR /dev/full .
.SH FILES
.B /dev/full
(character device, major 1, minor 7)
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B ENOSPC
Any write-like operation.
.TP
.B ENOTTY
Any
.BR ioctl (2)
request.
.TP
.B EINVAL
Any
.BR mmap (2)
attempt.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR null (4),
.BR zero (4),
.BR poll (2),
.BR mmap (2)
